@@ -13,6 +13,14 @@ export JAVA_HOME=$(mx --dynamicimports /substratevm graalvm-home)
 
 To enable the LLVM backend, pass the `--tool:llvm-backend` option to the `native-image` command. 
 
+## Limitations
+
+With the LLVM backend, the Graal compiler's vectorization optimizations remain enabled, but vector memory and arithmetic operations use scalar widths.
+LLVM may vectorize the generated bitcode during compilation.
+
+The LLVM backend does not support the [Foreign Function and Memory (FFM) API](https://www.graalvm.org/latest/reference-manual/native-image/native-code-interoperability/ffm-api/).
+Native Image disables FFM support when you select `--tool:llvm-backend`.
+
 ## Debugging Options
 
 * `-H:TempDirectory=`: specifies where the files generated by Native Image will be saved. The LLVM files are saved under `SVM-<timestamp>/llvm` in this directory.
